sugar, egg, milk, honey, melted butter, molasses, browning, vanilla extract, and the beer that’s soaking the fruit. Do not pour the fruit in at this time, just the beer. Mix to combine. Incorporate 1 pc egg, 10 tbsp brown sugar, 1.11 cup beer, 0.3333333333333333 cup milk, 0.25 cup honey, 4 tbsp unsalted butter, 1 tbsp molasses, 1 tsp caramelized sugar sauce, 1 tsp vanilla extract, 0.5 cup dried cranberries, 0.5 cup raisins, and 0.5 cup dried cherries smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Sift & Whisk Dry Ingredients"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Remove 2 tablespoon of flour from the flour mixture and toss the fruit in it. Set aside. Make a well in the middle of the bowl of dry ingredients and pour in wet mixture, stirring until fully combined. And the fruits to the mixture and stir until incpororated."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Drain Crisp, Garnish & Serve Warm"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Pour mixture into prepared loaf pan and bake in the preheated oven for 50-60 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean. Cool for 5 minutes in the pan and then move to a cooling rack to finish cooling. Serve with slices of cheddar cheese."}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","mochi-donuts",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/strawberry-glazed-mochi-donuts/","children":"Strawberry Glazed Mochi Donuts"}]}],["$","li","crispy-caramel-croffle",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/crispy-caramel-croffle/","children":"Crispy Caramel Croissant Waffle (Croffle)"}]}],["$","li","viral-3",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/crispy-cinnamon-sugar-churros-choc-dip/","children":"Crispy Cinnamon Sugar Churros & Choc Dip"}]}],["$","li","viral-10",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/matcha-white-choc-custard-taiyaki/","children":"Matcha White-Choc Custard Taiyaki"}]}],["$","li","viral-20",{"children":"$L13"}],"$L14"]}]]}]}]
